= The Unreasonable Effectiveness of Mathematics in the Natural Sciences / 数学在自然科学中不可思议的有效性

#html.p(id: "en-G001")[#text("Wigner asks why mathematics developed through abstract reasoning works so well in describing physical phenomena. The usefulness itself becomes the object of inquiry.")]

#zh(id: "G001")[#text("维格纳追问：通过抽象推理发展起来的数学，为什么能如此有效地描述物理现象？有效性本身成为了需要解释的问题。")]

#html.p(id: "en-G002")[#text("Distinguish fitting a formula to known observations from finding that a mathematical framework reaches further than expected. The latter makes the puzzle especially striking.")]

#zh(id: "G002")[#text("应当区分两件事：为已知观察拟合一个公式，以及发现某个数学框架适用的范围超出了预期。后一种情形使这个疑问格外鲜明。")]

#html.p(id: "en-G003")[#text("This is a conceptual essay, so read its examples as invitations to examine the relationship between mathematical concepts and physical laws. It is not a technical proof of universal mathematical coverage.")]

#zh(id: "G003")[#text("这是一篇概念性的文章，可以借它的例子考察数学概念与物理定律的关系。它不是一份证明数学能够包揽一切现象的技术证明。")]

#html.p(id: "en-G004")[#text("Reading question: does successful prediction fully explain why a model works? Compare practical confidence in a theory with an explanation of its remarkable success.")]

#zh(id: "G004")[#text("阅读时可以追问：预测成功，是否就完全解释了一个模型为什么有效？可以比较对理论的实用信心，与对其惊人成功的解释。")]
